{# The charge region of the invoice create screen raising an invoice AGAINST A SALES ORDER — the
   `chargeTemplate` admin/invoice/create.html.twig delegates to.

   A charge is a quantified row like any other (#539 stage 5). A flat fee is a row of quantity 1:
   bill 0.4 of it here and 0.6 stays on the order for the next invoice. Nothing is apportioned — the
   remainder is offered, and the person raising the invoice decides. Clearing a row's quantity leaves
   that charge off this invoice entirely.

   This is the half of the sales-order field being set that could not be a parameter: these rows DRAW
   DOWN charges that already exist and post `charges[N][slug|quantity|amount]`, while the standalone
   screen MINTS them and posts `charge_lines[N][...]` through the shared charge row. Two contracts,
   read by two saves — not two spellings of one.

   The whole section is absent where the order has nothing left to charge, which is why the caller
   passes no rows rather than this file hiding an empty table.

   Rendered with {chargeRows}. #}
{% if chargeRows is not empty %}
    <h2>Charges to invoice</h2>
    <p class="lead" style="margin:0 0 12px;">
        Shipping, fees and discounts are quantified rows too. A flat charge is one whole unit: bill
        part of it here and the rest stays on the order. Clear a quantity to leave that charge off
        this invoice. The amount follows the quantity unless you type one over it. Nothing here is
        apportioned for you.
    </p>
    <div class="wide-table-wrap">
        <table class="wide-price-table invoice-charge-table">
            <thead>
                <tr>
                    <th>Charge</th>
                    <th>Kind</th>
                    <th style="text-align:right;">Ordered</th>
                    <th style="text-align:right;">Invoiced</th>
                    <th>Now</th>
                    <th>Amount</th>
                </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
                {% for i, charge in chargeRows %}
                    <tr class="invoice-charge-row">
                        <td data-label="Charge">
                            {{ charge.label }}
                            <input type="hidden" name="charges[{{ i }}][slug]" value="{{ charge.slug }}">
                            <small class="field-hint">${{ charge.unitAmount|amount }} per whole charge</small>
                        </td>
                        <td data-label="Kind">{{ charge.type }}</td>
                        <td data-label="Ordered" style="text-align:right;">{{ charge.ordered }}</td>
                        <td data-label="Invoiced" style="text-align:right;">{{ charge.invoiced }}</td>
                        <td data-label="Now">
                            <input class="form-control" type="number" step="0.01" min="0" max="{{ charge.remaining }}"
                                   name="charges[{{ i }}][quantity]" value="{{ charge.remaining }}">
                        </td>
                        <td data-label="Amount">
                            <input class="form-control" type="text" name="charges[{{ i }}][amount]" value="{{ charge.amount|number_format(2, '.', '') }}">
                        </td>
                    </tr>
                {% endfor %}
            </tbody>
        </table>
    </div>
{% endif %}
